    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d227">

                <pb facs="0391" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15/834: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-17T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 17,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 17—11:30
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>123. Drummond telephoned this morning that during Lugano session the three powers
                    mostly interested, namely Great Britain, France and Germany, agreed to advise
                    Loudon to call meeting of the Preparatory Commission between the 8th and 15th of
                    April (the latest date to which Stresemann<anchor n="30" xml:id="d227-f1"/>
                    would agree). Drummond stated that the date was not made definite since they
                    recognized that the members <pb facs="0392" n="264" xml:id="pg264"/> of the
                    American delegation coming from the United States might desire to remain home
                    over Easter which occurs March 31. He asked me to obtain an unofficial
                    expression of opinion from you as to which time would be most convenient for the
                    opening of the session between these dates.</p>
                <p>Copy to Gibson.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d227-f1" n="30" xml:id="d227-f1-content">
                <p>Gustav Stresemann, German Minister of Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
